# spark models.env -- the curated model table: open licenses only, each row
# proven on the line (CLAUDE.md's rule) before it lands here. This is the
# only list SITE_AI_MODEL=auto and SITE_EMBER_MODEL=auto read.
# `./bootstrap.sh --list-models` shows it with a RAM verdict and marks the
# picks (* spark, + ember); auto picks the pair by the 60% RAM budget: the
# smallest row beside the largest that fits, else the largest alone. Every
# row: file url bytes sha256 ram_gb, where ram_gb = file size x 1.1 + 1.5,
# rounded up (weights plus context and runtime). Names: MODEL_<NAME>, shown
# lower-case with dashes.
#
# Two more lists sit beside this one: `embers.env` (conversational models
# with a purpose -- Apache-2.0/MIT/etc only, like this one) and
# `community.env` (any license, named, untested, at your own risk). A row
# in either is a pull request; see their own headers for the shape.
#
# Sizes and sha256 come from Hugging Face's LFS metadata; bootstrap.sh
# verifies the sha256 before a file is kept. All Q4_K_M unless noted.
